window.docContents[133].resolve({"/#Core-C______":{"contents":"Core C++ is a subset of C++17 with an LL(1) grammar and no undefined behaviour, the core language of the course 09022, Linguagens de Programação, at IME. This blueprint holds the lexer, the grammar, and the typing and evaluation rules in natural semantics, in the sequent style of Kahn (1987), and points each rule to the Lean code that implements it in core-cpp/CoreCpp/. The source, the interpreter and this blueprint live in the repository github.com/ChristianoBraga/corecpp. One chapter per UD of the syllabus, one node per construction or nonterminal, and a final chapter with the planned constructions that have no rules yet. The seven units are written.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"","header":"Core C++","id":"/#Core-C______"}});